  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting Pradhan Mantri Skilling and Employability Transformation through Upgraded ITIs</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The development objective of the Supporting Pradhan Mantri Skilling and Employability Transformation Through Upgraded Industrial Training Institutes (ITIs) Program for India is to increase the number and employability of graduates and strengthen the governance and management of supported ITIs. The government Program has two main components: (i) transforming the governance and management of ITIs to deliver quality and demand-driven training to youth at scale, ensuring that graduates are employable and better skilled for jobs and entrepreneurship, to contribute to employment and productivity; and (ii) transforming five National Skill Training Institute (NSTIs) to become premier institutes for vocational teacher training and research to improve teacher training programs. The government program has two components. The first component of the program will reorganize 1,000 government ITIs into hub-and-spoke governance arrangements and upgrade them for improved and diversified trades primarily in the priority sectors. The second component will aim to create similar governance and management changes in five selected NSTIs. Program-for-Results (PforR) activities are grouped under three interrelated results areas (RAs): RA1: transforming ITIs for higher performance; RA2: creating a subnational enabling environment for the ITI ecosystem; and RA3: strengthening national capacity in policy coordination, program management, and monitoring and evaluation.</narrative>
  </description>
